    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** anchoring the outfield, serving as our highest-upside plays. **Kyle Tucker** (85.72) benefits from a prime matchup against Sugano, where a favorable park factor and a 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set elevate his floor significantly. **Andy Pages** (75.63) mirrors this advantage, as his neutral platoon status is mitigated by the same park and skill-based tailwinds, making him a cornerstone for offensive production. Additionally, **Drake Baldwin** earns a high score of 72.04 by virtue of his leadoff spot and a strong xwOBA, turning the UTIL slot into a high-efficiency engine against Ober.\n\nMid-tier decisions across the infield remain defensive in nature as we navigate tougher matchups. **Liam Hicks**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill** all hover in the low 50s; while they aren\u2019t projected for ceiling games, they provide reliable baseline production. We are closely monitoring **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 15% platoon penalty against McClanahan restricts his score, though his foundational talent keeps him in the starting nine. **Miguel Vargas** also sees a moderate impact from the 3.74 xERA of Imanaga, but his elite 0.383 xwOBA ensures he remains an essential part of the order.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci**, who narrowly missed the cutoff with a score of 39.73. Ultimately, the decision to sit him was driven by the strict 40.0 floor; his left-on-left disadvantage against Imanaga and a lower-leverage #7 batting position made him a liability compared to the higher-floor options currently starting. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are leaning heavily on our healthy core to bridge the gap in stolen bases and counting stats. Owners should keep a close eye on the weather and confirmed lineups for the middle infielders to ensure no late-hour shifts disrupt our calculated approach to game-cap preservation.",
